<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('partials/head') %></head>
<body data-page="join">
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<main id="main">
  <section class="hero" style="padding:64px 0; background-image: url('/assets/icso-background.jpg');">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Auditions</p>
      <h1>Join ICSO</h1>
      <p class="lede">Information about the audition process is below. We look forward to hearing you play!</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
  <div class="wrap grid cols-2" style="align-items:start;column-gap:64px;">
    <div class="faq reveal">
      <h2>ICSO Auditions</h2>
        <p>ICSO is a fully auditioned orchestra. Audition slots are 10 minutes long. 5 minutes are for your own-choice piece (unaccompanied), and the rest is for some sight-reading and a small discussion with the audition panel.</p>
        <p>To audition for ICSO, sign up at the start of the academic year. Best of luck!</p>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I sign up for an audition?</summary>
        <p>Come find us at the <a href="https://www.imperialcollegeunion.org/">Welcome Fair</a> to sign up or check out our <a href="https://www.instagram.com/icsorchestra/">Instagram</a> page for the sign-up form (released at the start of the academic year).</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What grade should I be?</summary>
        <p>There is no required grade to join. The average standard of members is around Grade 8, and amongst us are several ex-members of the National Youth Orchestra, as well as graduates of the junior conservatoires.</p>
        <p>But don't be put off - anyone is welcome to audition!</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>When are auditions held?</summary>
        <p>Auditions for 2026 will run in the first two weeks of the academic year.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who will be on the audition panel?</summary>
        <p>Auditions are held jointly with <a href="https://www.imperialcollegeunion.org/activities/a-to-z/orchestra-sinfonietta">Imperial College Sinfonietta</a>, so the conductors and committee chairs for both IC Sinfonietta and ICSO will be present. Section leaders may also be present for some auditions.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will I be able to warm up beforehand?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Arrive 10-15 minutes before your audition to warm up on your instrument. A practice room will be provided. To book more time in a practice room, contact the <a href="https://www.imperial.ac.uk/music-and-arts/music/practice-rooms/">Blyth Centre</a> as soon as possible.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will there be an accompanist?</summary>
        <p>No. We ask everybody to audition without accompaniment to keep auditions fair for those who don't have an accompanist. Your piece does not have to originally be written as an unaccompanied work.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How long should my own-choice piece be?</summary>
        <p>Around 5 minutes long. The piece can be an excerpt from a larger work, if you wish. Just make sure it shows off what you can do!</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>When will I hear the outcome?</summary>
        <p>For 2026, in the second week of term. Entry into ICSO can be incredibly competitive, so don't worry if you don't get in the first time: you can try again later in the year if a spot opens, or at the start of the following year.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I'm not an Imperial student. Can I still audition?</summary>
        <p>Yes. We welcome external students to audition and get involved too.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I have another question...</summary>
        <p>Feel free to come and ask us any other questions that you might have at ICSO's stall at the <a href="https://www.imperialcollegeunion.org/">Welcome Fair</a> at the start of the academic year.</p>
        <p>If there's anything else we can help with, please <a href="/contact">contact</a> us.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <div>
        <img src="/assets/strings-rach-prok-2025.jpg" alt="ICSO strings in concert" style="border-radius:2px;border:1px solid var(--line);">
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--ink-soft); text-align:center; font-style:italic;">
          <b>ICSO strings in concert, Cadogan Hall (March 2025)</b><br>ICSO performing Prokofiev's Symphony No. 5, conducted by Oliver Gooch
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:20px;">
        <br>
        <h2>Concerto Performances</h2>
        <p>ICSO and <a href="https://www.imperialcollegeunion.org/activities/a-to-z/orchestra-sinfonietta">IC Sinfonietta</a> provide opportunities for those keen to be considered for a concerto performance, typically with one concerto soloist joining each orchestra per term. Concerto performances with other Imperial music ensembles may be arranged, but on a case-by-case basis.</p>
        <p>Concerto auditions are held once a year in the Spring Term for performance in the following academic year. You will be asked to play for a total of 10-15 minutes across all movements of the concerto. Unlike the regular auditions to play in the orchestra, an accompanist <i>will</i> be provided for the concerto auditions (but you may bring your own if you wish).</p>
        <p>Please <a href="https://icso.uk/?page_id=55">get in touch</a> if you'd like to learn more about concerto auditions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="wrap" style="margin-top:24px;text-align:center;font-weight:600;">We look forward to meeting you and listening to your audition. Good luck!</p>
</section>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
